  "title": "Four gasket levels force the standing wave",
  "subject": "Which three-bit laws symmetric in two corners reproduce themselves on consecutive Sierpinski gasket levels",
  "conclusion": "A three-bit law symmetric in its two non-base corners reproduces itself on the Sierpinski gaskets of levels 2 to 5 exactly when it is a standing wave, a product, an equal-corner law or one of two frozen laws, and then it does so at every level. Fewer levels admit impostors: a whole curve at levels 2 and 3, and 16 complex laws at levels 2 to 4.",
